Microtrust legacy Android 10 transport
=====================================

Imported from Lenovo tab_m10_fhd_plus_opensource_tb-x606m_s000213_200302_bmain,
kernel-4.9/drivers/misc/mediatek/teei/280. Original copyright and GPL notices
are retained. Selected with CONFIG_MICROTRUST_TEE_VERSION="280".

The X606F Android 10 stock kernel exposes create_cmd_buff, invoke_fastcall,
register_soter_irq_handler and the 20-UUID configuration ioctl. These are
the legacy message-buffer and 32-byte notification queue interfaces. The
runtime config's "300" string does not identify the secure firmware's ABI.
The donor 300 transport instead sends b400000c to an ATF which rejects it.

4.19 adaptations:
- CPU hotplug state callbacks replace the removed CPU notifier interface.
- system_transition_mutex replaces the 4.9 power management mutex.
- DMA-buf mapping, signal includes, bootprof and Clang operand widths follow
  the 4.19 interfaces.
- isee_* names and isee_tee core name avoid the generic Linux TEE symbols.
  Userspace device names and the legacy wire protocols are preserved.

See the workspace notes/port/2026-10-08-android10-tee-compat.md for measured
firmware evidence, build commands and device validation. The 300 donor
implementation remains available independently.
